#>wonder_trial_gap
?["Is a gap between two terms a join: company, an order, or nothing a reader should keep?"]{
 #:depth #!syntax ~#lens(comparison)
 ~#readings: ["company: a gap is a comma left out, and *wonders{ @a $b #c } holds three members", "order: a gap is a sequence, each term read after the one before", "phrase: a gap joins words into one part, as prose does, and only a mark or a brace starts a new one", "axis: a gap is the innermost step of a walk, so m{ 1 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 1 } is a matrix with a gap along a row and a semicolon between rows, and each looser separator is one more dimension", "nothing: a body's first term is its part and the remainder is unread (seed's line reader today)"]
 ~#grounded: "asyndeton and parataxis: clauses set side by side with no conjunction (I came, I saw) are still read as joined, and listeners tell a list from a phrase by the shape of its members, not by a word between them"
 ~#interactive: "a canvas draws three members in a ring or one phrase on a line; a drag can lift $b out only when it is a part; a writer adds a member by typing a gap and a word"
 ~#asked: "the owner, 2026-11-09: the space separator could be traversed, with some benefit to describing compression or matrices"
 ~#forms: ["*wonders{ @a $b #c }", "*wonders{ @a, $b, #c }", "~berries{ boonberry baneberry }", "?{ where will the ice sit }", "x{ a.b c.d }", "x{ a, b c }", "m{ 1 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 1 }", "steps{ X . . x . . . . }"]
 ~#pairs: ["*wonders{ @a $b #c } / *wonders{ @a, $b, #c }: a gap or a comma", "~berries{ boonberry baneberry } / ?{ where will the ice sit }: two members or one phrase", "x{ a, b c } / x{ a, b, c }: a pair inside a company or three alike"]
 ~#readers_today: .{ seed: "the parser reads every gap in a body as the boundary between expressions, prose included, and keeps one flat sequence with its separators in order, so m{ 1 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 1 } is nine expressions whose separators read gap gap ; gap gap ; gap gap; the line reader reads the first term and leaves the others unread, and reads that matrix as three rows with no cells (journal 2026-11-09-reader-agreement)", site_reader: "3 single-line bodies with terms side by side", second_consumer: "230 of its 1,620 single-line bodies set terms side by side, 149 of them marked terms only", factshift: "_", agent: "_" }
 ~#home: ~"../syntax-hardware-alignment/wip.spw"
 ~#judgment: _
 ~#answer: _
 $%[company, order, phrase, axis, nothing]
}

